cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software and the accompanying study, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software
title: "EQLI / Entangletronica: Electrostatic Quantum-Lens Interferometry in InGaAs 2DEGs"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible split-step Schroedinger simulations of a single flying electron
  through a gate-defined double-slit interferometer in a ballistic 2DEG, with a
  programmable electrostatic phase lens, a Poisson-Thomas-Fermi voltage mapping,
  a stochastic dephasing budget, and a scalable two-input XOR gate proposal.
  Companion to the EQLI preprint.
authors:
  - family-names: "Terzi"
    given-names: "Fabrizio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9131-3520"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
keywords:
  - flying-electron logic
  - quantum interferometry
  - two-dimensional electron gas (2DEG)
  - split-step Fourier method
  - electrostatic phase gate
  - quantum simulation
